: "Bug 1730070: Update DDG logo. r=Standard8, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125145", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/data/content/tippytop/favicons/duckduckgo-com.ico", "browser/components/newtab/data/content/tippytop/images/duckduckgo-com@2x.png", "browser/components/newtab/data/content/tippytop/images/duckduckgo-com@2x.svg", "browser/components/newtab/data/content/tippytop/top_sites.json", "browser/components/search/extensions/ddg/favicon.ico"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3f0a710a4ea771fc8270ab3d338642ff14a93865", "parents": ["09c409e77215ed9236772925b67c538ced8e6a32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722597 - prevent unwarranted error console spew \"Prompter: internal dialogs not available in this context.\". r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123211", "files": ["toolkit/components/prompts/src/Prompter.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bb3d6b773f65fac647e5277480b9c6a871487c96", "parents": ["3f0a710a4ea771fc8270ab3d338642ff14a93865"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dzmitry Malyshau \u003cdmalyshau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725854 - Check for the WebGPU pref before initializing the GPU process IPC side. r=aosmond, a=RyanVM", "files": ["gfx/ipc/CompositorOptions.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "widget/nsBaseWidget.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "989bde68af0951b0c1be25fb6304f4b358849979", "parents": ["bb3d6b773f65fac647e5277480b9c6a871487c96"], "tags": []}], "date": 1631894485, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "58": {"changesets": [{"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1659101 - fix intermittent failure in browser_preoloading_tab_moving.js, r=jaws, a=test-only\n\nSee discussion in the last few comments on the bug. If we don't wait for the correct URL\nto load in the browser, the SpecialPowers.spawn task can get aborted, which causes the\ntest to fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119518", "files": ["browser/modules/test/browser/browser.ini", "browser/modules/test/browser/browser_preloading_tab_moving.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dfbd4f95725232f60c26a9b01191f2d8b1008f93", "parents": ["989bde68af0951b0c1be25fb6304f4b358849979"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1673870 - [devtools] Fix browser_resources_getAllResources.js intermittent. r=ladybenko, a=test-only\n\nThe test was failing because we were getting cached messages\nfrom a worker that were emitted late.\nTo fix this, we create a dedicated document with workers\nonly when we need them and remove workers from fission_document.html.\nThis allows us to cleanup a few tests that were already working\naround the worker logs issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122326", "files": ["devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser.ini", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser_resources_console_messages.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser_resources_console_messages_navigation.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser_resources_console_messages_workers.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser_resources_getAllResources.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/browser_resources_target_switching.js", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/fission_document.html", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/fission_document_workers.html", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/fission_iframe.html", "devtools/shared/commands/resource/tests/fission_iframe_workers.html", "devtools/shared/commands/target/tests/test_worker.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b29e01b4dff14d92519ad49f21f42d28a8d32bb0", "parents": ["dfbd4f95725232f60c26a9b01191f2d8b1008f93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kashav Madan \u003ckshvmdn@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1677540 - Skip browser_async_remove_tab.js for non-SHIP, r=annyG, a=test-only\n\nThis fails in promiseOnHistoryReplaceEntry since the browser goes away before\nthe SpecialPowers task can resolve. This doesn't apply to SHIP since we listen\nfor history events in the parent instead for that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122486", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d64bfc87b67884daaa62f7718cfd885c4a1fb84b", "parents": ["b29e01b4dff14d92519ad49f21f42d28a8d32bb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1676524 - fix intermittent failures in browser_experimental_features_filter.js due to fluent races r=emilio a=test-only\n\nThe test overwrites a fluent-originating text content with its own,\nbut doesn't clear the fluent data-l10n-id attribute. As a result,\nif it tries to write the textContent before the data-l10n-id pass\nfrom fluent has run, fluent overwrites the textContent before we\ndo a search, and then the rest of the test gets bogus results\nbecause it matches against the wrong text content.\n\nThis patch fixes this by removing the data-l10n-id attribute so\nthe fluent pass doesn't try to put text in these elements\nanymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122659", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_experimental_features_filter.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1cf52cf714762b2d01b39b8ef013b641fe179f02", "parents": ["d64bfc87b67884daaa62f7718cfd885c4a1fb84b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1631901182, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "59": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D126091", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "464354ea46475b405d0bbd4d55148970e2711b05", "parents": ["1cf52cf714762b2d01b39b8ef013b641fe179f02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722544 - Allow SanitizeOnShutdown policy to be false. r=emalysz, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122031", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_simple_pref_policies.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "be6169423427ca7ee08cf4fc91cee84fcfeb4eb2", "parents": ["464354ea46475b405d0bbd4d55148970e2711b05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1726547 - Don't show VPN promo link if enterprise policy is active. r=groovecoder, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123113", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutPrivateBrowsingParent.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "94feed72e138c30f078b658cef49932a83049060", "parents": ["be6169423427ca7ee08cf4fc91cee84fcfeb4eb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729642 - patch 1 - Make shutdown of nsLanguageAtomService explicit instead of relying on ClearOnShutdown. r=platform-i18n-reviewers,dminor a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125587", "files": ["intl/locale/nsLanguageAtomService.cpp", "intl/locale/nsLanguageAtomService.h", "layout/build/nsLayoutStatics.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c0c30730a0630859010a4e784bfd714401389981", "parents": ["94feed72e138c30f078b658cef49932a83049060"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729642 - patch 2 - Make nsContentUtils hold a strong reference to the nsNameSpaceManager. r=emilio a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D125587\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125588", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "53441d71908fa3a7e72a22c0c2438315ed92f31a", "parents": ["c0c30730a0630859010a4e784bfd714401389981"], "tags": []}], "date": 1632161866, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "60": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729813 - Update rayon to pick up a newer crossbeam version in style/webrender. r=nical, a=RyanVM\n\nIt was downgraded to investigate some windows crashes which ended up\nbeing a crossbeam issue. So update it again to get fixes to some\ncrossbeam races.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D125051", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/LICENSE-APACHE", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/LICENSE-MIT", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/README.md", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/benches/crossbeam.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.4/examples/fibonacci.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-channel-0.4.